ph7
------------------------------------------
PH7 is a in-process software library that implements a highly-efficient
embeddable bytecode compiler and a virtual machine for the PHP programming
language.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libph7-devel-2.1.4-1bl2
  libph7_2-2.1.4-1bl2
  pkg-config-3.0.11-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://ph7.symisc.net/

Canonical download:
  https://symisc.net/downloads/ph7-amalgamation-2001004.zip

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack ph7-2.1.4-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./ph7-2.1.4-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/ph7-2.1.4-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/ph7-2.1.4-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libph7_2-2.1.4-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libph7-devel-2.1.4-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(ph7)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/ph7.README
  /usr/share/doc/ph7/license.txt

(libph7_2)
  /usr/bin/cygph7-2.dll

(libph7-devel)
  /usr/include/ph7.h
  /usr/lib/libph7.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/ph7.pc

------------------

Port Notes:

----- version 2.1.4-1bl2 -----
Rebuild with gcc-14.4.0

----- version 2.1.4-1bl1 -----
